        <body>
            <div xml:id="d130">

                <pb facs="0745" n="718" xml:id="pg718"/>

                <head>130. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in the Soviet
                        Union<anchor n="1" xml:id="d130-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">164262.</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1990-05-22T03:28:00+00:00">May 22, 1990,
                            0328Z</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Soviet Arms Control Experts Group</item>
                </list>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>(S) Entire Text.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Embassy should ask MFA for the
                        composition of the Soviet Arms Control Experts Group that is coming to
                        Washington this week pursuant to the agreement between Foreign Minister
                            Shevardnadze and Secretary
                            Baker, and the timing of their
                        arrival and departure.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>We consider this to be a continuation of the Karpov-Bartholomew
                        working group meetings in Moscow. We assume they will continue to address
                        the agenda discussed in Moscow, including the following issues: <list>
                            <label>—</label>
                            <item>Heavy ICBMs;</item>
                            <label>—</label>
                            <item>Mobile ICBM limits and
                                verification;</item>
                            <label>—</label>
                            <item>Backfire;</item>
                            <label>—</label>
                            <item>Non-circumvention;</item>
                            <label>—</label>
                            <item>ICBM warhead sublimit;</item>
                            <label>—</label>
                            <item>Phasing of reductions</item>
                        </list></item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>The group can also consider the bracketed text of the joint statement on
                        future negotiations and PPCM, both of
                        which are now being worked in Geneva.</item>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item>In addition, we also look forward to Soviet responses to the CFE ideas the US put forward in Moscow.</item>
                    <label>6.</label>
                    <item>As in Moscow, the purpose of this meeting would be to reach agreements on
                        these issues to recommend to ministers.</item>
                    <label>7.</label>
                    <item>You should confirm that Moscow has the same understanding of the
                        objectives of the experts session as Washington.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Baker</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
